# The app verifies every patch against the SHA-256 in manifest.json, hashing
# the bytes it downloads from raw.githubusercontent.com — which are git's
# stored blob, always LF.
#
# On Windows core.autocrlf=true rewrites checked-out files to CRLF. That
# changes their bytes, so a hash computed from the working tree does NOT match
# what clients download. Patch 2026.08.16.009 shipped three such hashes and
# broke updating for everyone until it was corrected.
#
# Pinning these files to LF keeps the working tree byte-identical to what is
# served, so hashing either one gives the same answer.
manifest.json text eol=lf
patches/*.json text eol=lf
verify-manifest.js text eol=lf
